.TH terminal-of-tinsel-stocking 1  "stocking " 
.SH NAME
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-stocking \- Look in your stocking: the creatures you\*(Aqve caught, your badges and records
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBterminal\-of\-tinsel stocking\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-pack\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Your stocking holds every creature you\*(Aqve caught by answering three questions about it, in the quiz or Guess the Guest, plus your badges and records. It\*(Aqs saved as JSON in your config directory; set TERMINAL_OF_TINSEL_HOME to keep it somewhere else.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the command\*(Aqs data as JSON instead of drawing it (errors become a JSON object on stderr)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Plain output: no colour, no emoji, ASCII borders (also set by NO_COLOR, or by piping)
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR \fI<PACK>\fR
Only use creatures from these packs, e.g. \-\-pack nordic,dickens
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-stocking\-reset(1)
